    "result_text": "Done. I agreed with the finding and fixed it.\n\n**Change made:**\n- Added `OwnerRegion.isKnownRegion(String)` \u2014 a `public static boolean` predicate that answers the region-membership question directly against `REGION_POSTCODES` (the known-region set), with a Javadoc stating the three codes.\n- `OwnerMapper.ownerSegment` now calls `OwnerRegion.isKnownRegion(locality(owner))` instead of inferring \"known\" from a non-null timezone lookup.\n\nThis puts the \"is this a known region\" logic in the documented single source of truth, makes the intent self-documenting, and decouples segmentation from the timezone table \u2014 so a future region added without a timezone mapping would be classified correctly rather than silently falling to `REGIONAL`.\n\nAcceptance behaviour is unchanged (the three known regions are identical in both tables today): the full suite is **BUILD SUCCESS**, 2/2 tests passing.",
