    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe `ownerSegment` method is placed well \u2014 it sits naturally alongside the other derivation helpers (`ageBand`, `salutation`, `contactPreference`, `timezone`) in the mapper, matches their shape, and the Javadoc mirrors the spec. The OpenAPI addition is consistent with the neighbouring fields. One structural issue:\n\n**\"Known region\" is derived by abusing the timezone table instead of asking the region domain.**\n`OwnerMapper.java:56-57` decides `metro` via `OwnerRegion.timezoneOfRegion(locality(owner)) != null`. The spec's actual question is \"is the locality one of the known regions (NSW/VIC/QLD)?\" \u2014 a region-membership question. Answering it through the timezone lookup is indirect and couples segment logic to an unrelated table:\n\n- It conflates two distinct facts (\"this region has an IANA timezone\" vs. \"this region is known\"). They coincide today only because `REGION_TIMEZONE` happens to key on exactly the same three codes as `REGION_POSTCODES`/`CITY_REGION`. A future region added to the postcode/city tables without a timezone mapping would silently be classified `REGIONAL`, and a maintainer reading `ownerSegment` would have no cue that it depends on the timezone table's completeness.\n- `OwnerRegion` is explicitly documented as the \"single source of truth for an owner's REGION code,\" and the mapper already delegates all other region work to it (`locality`, `timezone`, `regionOf`, `regionFromCustomerCode`). The \"is this a known region\" predicate belongs there too, not expressed as a side effect of a timezone call in the mapper.\n\nSuggested fix: add a small predicate to `OwnerRegion` (the single source of truth), e.g.\n\n```java\n/** Whether the region code is one of the known regions (NSW, VIC, QLD). */\npublic static boolean isKnownRegion(String region) {\n    return region != null && REGION_POSTCODES.containsKey(region);\n}\n```\n\nand have `ownerSegment` call `OwnerRegion.isKnownRegion(locality(owner))`. This puts the region-membership logic in the right unit, makes the intent self-documenting, and decouples segmentation from the timezone table.",
